.TH "EPX\-CATALOGS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-catalogs \- read and change catalogs
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx catalogs [flags]
epx catalogs [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads catalogs, visible or not. STATUS and VISIBLE are separate Emporix fields and can disagree. ROOT CATEGORIES counts the categories assigned directly to the catalog.
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the catalog.catalog_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx catalogs create"
Create a catalog.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx catalogs create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a catalog from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, shaped as \fBepx catalogs get ID \-o json\fR shows one: name and description (maps of languages to text), visibility, publishedSites and categoryIds (root categories); Emporix generates the id unless the body gives one. It answers with the id; an id that exists already is a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the catalog.catalog_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx catalogs delete"
Delete a catalog.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx catalogs delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the catalog ID, as \fBepx catalogs list\fR shows it.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the catalog.catalog_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx catalogs for\-category"
List the catalogs a category is assigned to.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx catalogs for\-category CATEGORY_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads catalogs, visible or not. STATUS and VISIBLE are separate Emporix fields and can disagree. ROOT CATEGORIES counts the categories assigned directly to the catalog. CATEGORY_ID is the id of a category assigned to catalogs directly, a root category (an unindented row of \fBepx category\-trees list\fR); a category below one, or an unknown id, lists nothing.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, STATUS, VISIBLE, FROM, TO, SITES, ROOT CATEGORIES.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
