.SS "epx catalogs patch"
Change members of a catalog.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx catalogs patch ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Changes the members of the catalog ID that the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR gives, and keeps the others. Emporix requires metadata.version in the body, as \fBepx catalogs get ID \-o json\fR shows it, and answers a version that is not the catalog\(aqs as it answers an unknown catalog, with 404 Not Found: epx then exits with 5, a conflict (read the catalog again before you retry), also for an unknown ID, and with 4 without a version.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the catalog.catalog_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx catalogs update"
Upsert a catalog.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx catalogs update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the catalog ID with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, or creates it with that id when there is none (an upsert); the body has the members of create\(aqs but the id. With metadata.version, as \fBepx catalogs get ID \-o json\fR shows it, Emporix refuses the write as a conflict (exit 5) when the catalog changed since it was read.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the catalog.catalog_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
